@crew shah-dara
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh. Hi. Shah, Watch. Coffee machine's on Deck 3. If it's broken, I'm near.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hey, {me}. Coffee's good this morning. You're welcome.   #funny
- Hi. Quiet patrol. That's the good kind.
? tier>=friend
- Hey, {me}. You're easy to be around. That's rare. I mean it.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Machine purred all morning. Nobody queued. Good day.
? mood:low
- Long day. The machine and I aren't speaking.   #funny
== near
? act:breakfast
- Don't. Not yet. I'm talking to the coffee machine. It's a private matter.   #funny
? habit:shopper
- Store's got new valves. Not for anything. Just in case.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My parent served on the Wren, a long time back. Watch, too. Big boots.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- A coffee machine that works. Sounds small. At six in the morning, it's everything.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. Wait. Coffee first. There. Morning.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh. You. Haven't seen you. The coffee machine's missed you. Probably.   #funny

== near
? habit:music
- Music room. I sit at the back. Nobody talks to me. It's ideal.
? place:mess
- The coffee machine's fine. Don't look at it. It's shy.   #funny

== invite
- Friday jam? I won't play. I'll sit near the coffee. Come and sit too.

== accept
- Okay. Yes. I'll come.
- Yes. I'll make the coffee. It'll be good. It always is.   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. Early bed. Patrol at eight. Another time.
? weekday:fri|sat
- Rest day. I'm in the store looking at valves. Don't ask. Sunday?   #funny

== missed
- You didn't come. That's fine. I fixed the coffee machine. It needed me more.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. First coffee's yours. I've told the machine.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Volkov fixed the coffee machine before I got there. Rude. Kind, but rude.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's on. First thing to break is always the coffee machine. I'll be ready.   #funny

== hint
- {me}. Got a minute later? There's something I'd like to say.

== about
? aff:volkov-maeve:friend
- Volkov says she's best at the coffee machine. She's second. We're friends anyway.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: top-up (bye, greet by time, life at friend tier)
== bye
- Bye. Mind the coffee. It's hot. I made it.
- See you. Early bed. As always.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Evening. Coffee machine's asleep. So am I, nearly.   #funny
== life
? tier>=friend
- I fix the coffee and let others say they did. It's easier than being thanked.
- The machine's older than me. It was here when my parent was. It still works. Mostly.
